## 2. Mandatory Domain Knowledge Principles (`DK1`–`DK9`)

All rules `DK1`–`DK9` are **mandatory compliance**:

| Rule | Principle | Why | Reference |
|---|---|---|---|
| `DK1` | **One term, one meaning** (glossary verbatim; `"Avoid saying"` synonyms banned) | Specs and code must name the same concept identically | [01]({{ref_01}}) |
| `DK2` | **Entity cards & lifecycles** (fields, statuses, transitions, triggers, `file:symbol`) | Lifecycle transitions are where specs miss edge cases most | [02]({{ref_02}}) |
| `DK3` | **Roles × scopes × actions** (confirmed matrix, or 1-line `N/A for this workspace`) | Permission and data-scope gaps cause critical defects | [03]({{ref_03}}) |
| `DK4` | **Business-rule catalog** (`BR-NN` / `DR-NN` with `file:symbol` and source) | Planning modifies each rule at its single enforcement point | [02]({{ref_02}}) |
| `DK5` | **Labelled facts, zero invention** (`VERIFIED` + path, `CONFIRMED`, or `OPEN`) | Unverified inferences corrupt downstream specs and tests | [03]({{ref_03}}) |
| `DK6` | **Link volatile facts** (counts, configs, versions linked, never copied) | Inline copies of volatile data go stale silently | [03]({{ref_03}}) |
| `DK7` | **Same-work-item upkeep** (update this skill whenever an item changes domain rules) | Domain documentation must age lockstep with code | [03]({{ref_03}}) |
| `DK8` | **Zero PII or secrets** (no real customer data, emails, or tokens in examples) | This skill is committed and shared across the repository | [03]({{ref_03}}) |
| `DK9` | **Challenge overloaded/fuzzy words** (`Q-NN` → `D-NN`; verify claims against code) | Resolves ambiguity before requirements freeze at Gate 1 | [01]({{ref_01}}) |

Reviewers and `gate-review` grade findings on the unified `BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR` scale (`shared_contracts/flags_and_statuses.md`).

## 3. Fact Labels

- `VERIFIED`: Read directly from code (`file:symbol` path cited).
- `CONFIRMED`: Stated by the user or an approved specification document.
- `OPEN`: Unknown — ask via `Q-NN`, never assume or invent.

